From: suvojeet-sengupta <suvojitsengupta21@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:02:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: Let Settings and system_server use the PIHooks
 disable props

The Play Integrity Fix switch in Settings writes
persist.sys.pihooks.disable.gms_props, but only shell may set
pih_disable_prop. Settings runs as system_app, so the set is denied,
SystemProperties.set() throws and Settings crashes as soon as the
switch is turned on.

system_server isn't an appdomain either, so PIHooks there can't read
the props at all: every app launch logs an avc denial and "Access
denied finding property" and it always sees them as unset.
---
 sepolicy/private/pihooks.te | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sepolicy/private/pihooks.te

diff --git a/sepolicy/private/pihooks.te b/sepolicy/private/pihooks.te
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..636194f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sepolicy/private/pihooks.te
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# The Play Integrity Fix switch in Settings sets persist.sys.pihooks.disable.*
+set_prop(system_app, pih_disable_prop)
+
+# PIHooks also runs in system_server and reads them there
+get_prop(system_server, pih_disable_prop)
-- 
